SUMMARY:City of Toronto Archives:  Private Tour (Arts & Culture focus)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n**The Toronto Archives** preserves and
  makes accessible government records\, which provide evidence of the decis
 ions\, policies\, and activities of the City of Toronto. The Archives also
  collects non-government records from people and organizations that have m
 ade significant contributions to the development and history of Toronto.\n
 \nWe will have a **PRIVATE** ('behind the scenes' TOUR at the Archives--wi
 th a focus on the historical past of Toronto's arts & culture history)\n\n
 The Archives has more than a million photographs in its collection. The ea
 rliest date from 1856.\n\nGovernment Office. Government Hours.\n\n**PLEASE
  note the date/time when you sign up. Check your calendars.**\n\n*Friday S
 eptember 11th* (2pm-3:30pm) ***FREE***\n\nSpadina/Dupont area (Short walk 
 from either Dupont TTC or Spadina TTC)\n\n20 spots ONLY.\n\nhttps://www.to
 ronto.ca/city-government/accountability-operations-customer-service/access
 -city-information-or-records/city-of-toronto-archives/\n\n(We recently had
  another TOUR here--and it was quite exceptional. The information shared w
 ith us 'ties' many of our recent historical walks together--visually)
